 arithmetic computation","origin":"explicit","start_byte":468},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":613,"interpretation":"avoid floating point","origin":"explicit","start_byte":592},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":1041,"interpretation":"unbounded mathematical integers","origin":"explicit","start_byte":970},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":3628,"interpretation":"preserved S2 identity","origin":"explicit","start_byte":2085},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":4264,"interpretation":"mandatory source delivery","origin":"explicit","start_byte":4060},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":4326,"interpretation":"formal source contract","origin":"explicit","start_byte":4265},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":4496,"interpretation":"exact source semantics cannot be replaced","origin":"explicit","start_byte":4327},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":4928,"interpretation":"operational source-only classification","origin":"explicit","start_byte":4775},{"document_hash":"sha256:7e8c0d17e78afc93ed267ed2738c4d8d2f739a551f7fe20ff302cecbf8fcd83b","document_ref":"tier2:tier2-source-facets-004:A23","end_byte":6207,"interpretation":"exact S2 source facets and value_required=false","origin":"explicit","start_byte":5156}],"state":"INTERPRETED","statement":"The canonical program.vscore.json entry solve of arity 1 uses exact unbounded mathematical integer arithmetic without floating point when evaluating the floor-sum specification, including arbitrarily large signed a and b. Its formal source contract requires typed_total, deterministic, input_preserved, no_external_io, no_floating_point, pure_data and restricted_runtime_only under normative Lean vscore-semantics/0.3. S2 is operational and source-only, while O1 and O2 retain the complete functional value formula and universal implementation refinement."}],"schema_version":"0.1"}